{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRootLabelling","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoTransport","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoPairSaddle","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmInversion"],"declarations":73,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.envelopeS_total_concrete_final","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.envelopeS_total_concrete_final","kind":"theorem","line":1134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L1134-L1156","doc":"**The transport, unconditionally.**\n\n    envelopeS Yreal Ypair.1 Ypair.2 π = envelopeS Yreal Ypair.1 Ypair.2 0 + π²\n\nGap A, closed. Every hypothesis is discharged: the labelling is constructed, its\nbranch routing settled, `VSide` and the two log sums proved at it, `heⱼ` pinned by\n`k = 0` in four regimes, continuity carried across the cut at `φ = π` by\n`continuousAt_re_cLiTwoExt`, and the collision both located (IVT) and shown\nunique (a quartic with one minimum).\n\n⚠ **This is not the sum rule.** `S(0) = −3π²/2` *is* the 5₂ sum rule and\n`S(0) = 3·S(π)`, so `S(π) − S(0) = π²` **reformulates** it. Closing Gap A moves a\nnamed gap inside a proved chain; it does not move the headline.\n\n**The 5₂ sum rule is PROVED**: `QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoComplexPentagon.fiveTwo_saddle_sum_rule`\nand `fiveTwoSaddleSumRule_holds`, sorry-free, standard axioms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exists_collision","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exists_collision","kind":"theorem","line":1123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L1123-L1132","doc":"**The collision EXISTS**, by the intermediate value theorem — and both ends\nare already theorems: `pairDisc 0 < 0` (the pair is complex at `φ = 0`) and\n`pairDisc π > 0` (it is real at `φ = π`, from the cubic). Nothing numeric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.envelopeS_total_concrete_of_unique_collision","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.envelopeS_total_concrete_of_unique_collision","kind":"theorem","line":1109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L1109-L1121","doc":"**The transport at the concrete labelling, with continuity supplied.**\n\n`S(π) − S(0) = π²` now rests on exactly one thing: that the collision `φ₀` is the\n**only** zero of `pairDisc` on the open arc. That is a statement about a quartic\nin `cos φ` — Route 32 measures its unique root at `c* = −0.7422176659` — and it\nis carried as a hypothesis rather than assumed, because measuring the number of\nroots of a quartic on a grid is exactly the shape of argument this lane has had\nto retract twice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairDisc_eq_zero_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairDisc_eq_zero_unique","kind":"theorem","line":1082,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L1082-L1107","doc":"**`hcoll`, proved.** At most one zero of `pairDisc` on `Icc 0 π`, hence on\nthe open arc. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.strictMonoOn_realRootPath","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.strictMonoOn_realRootPath","kind":"theorem","line":1058,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L1058-L1080","doc":"**`t` is strictly increasing in `φ` on `[0,π]`**, which is what turns\nuniqueness in `t` into uniqueness in `φ`. Two signs: `dt/dc < 0` (numerator\n`−2t(1−t) < 0` over a denominator `≥ 7/4`) and `dc/dφ = −sin φ < 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.strictMonoOn_collQuartic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.strictMonoOn_collQuartic","kind":"theorem","line":1046,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L1046-L1056","doc":"`E` is strictly increasing above `1/2`. The quadratic factor `t² − t + 3` has\ndiscriminant `−11`, so it never vanishes and never changes the sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_collQuartic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_collQuartic","kind":"theorem","line":1031,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L1031-L1044","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairDisc_mul_eq_collQuartic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairDisc_mul_eq_collQuartic","kind":"theorem","line":1015,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L1015-L1029","doc":"**The reduction.** A consequence of `unitCubic c t = 0` alone — Route 39 G1\nchecks it at five values of `c` *outside* `[−1,1]`, so nothing about the arc is\nsmuggled in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.collQuartic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.collQuartic","kind":"def","line":1012,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L1012-L1013","doc":"`E t = t⁴ − 2t³ + 7t² − 6t + 1`, the quartic `pairDisc` reduces to. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuousOn_envelopeS_concrete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuousOn_envelopeS_concrete","kind":"theorem","line":984,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L984-L988","doc":"**`hcont`** — the last hypothesis of `envelopeS_total_concrete`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuousAt_envelopeS_concrete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuousAt_envelopeS_concrete","kind":"theorem","line":915,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L915-L982","doc":"**`hcont`.** `envelopeS` is continuous at every point of `Icc 0 π`, endpoint\nincluded — which is where `continuousAt_re_cLiTwoExt` earns its place: at `φ = π`\nthe arguments `x·Ypair.2` and `Ypair.2/x` are both `−Ypair.2 π > 1`, sitting\n**on** Li₂'s cut, and no continuity statement about `cLiTwoExt` itself is true\nthere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuousAt_arcX","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuousAt_arcX","kind":"theorem","line":913,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L913-L913","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuousAt_Yreal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuousAt_Yreal","kind":"theorem","line":910,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L910-L911","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairDisc_zero_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairDisc_zero_neg","kind":"theorem","line":900,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L900-L908","doc":"At `φ = 0` the pair is complex: `β = t − 2 < 0`, and `pairBeta_pos` says that\nforces `pairDisc < 0`. Needed because the real-branch statements would otherwise\nhave to be argued at a point where they are false. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.neg_Ypair_mem_slitPlane_all","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.neg_Ypair_mem_slitPlane_all","kind":"theorem","line":891,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L891-L898","doc":"`−Ypair ∈ slitPlane` on the whole arc: by `Im ≠ 0` before the collision, by\n`Re < 0` at and after it. The two disjuncts, and neither covers both regimes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.notCut_Yreal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.notCut_Yreal","kind":"theorem","line":880,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L880-L889","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.notCut_Ypair_snd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.notCut_Ypair_snd","kind":"theorem","line":866,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L866-L878","doc":"The `snd` analogue of `notCut_Ypair_fst`, and the same for the real branch —\nboth on the **closed** left endpoint, where `VSide` is unavailable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arcX_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arcX_pi","kind":"theorem","line":863,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L863-L864","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.Ypair_pi_bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.Ypair_pi_bracket","kind":"theorem","line":840,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L840-L859","doc":"The endpoint values, bracketed. `Ypair.2 π < −1` is `β > 2`, i.e. `t > 0`.\n`Ypair.1 π > −1` is the one that needs the cubic: it is `√d > t`, i.e.\n`t² + t − 1 > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairDisc_pi_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairDisc_pi_pos","kind":"theorem","line":828,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L828-L838","doc":"`pairDisc π > 0`: the pair is REAL at the endpoint. `t·(t+2)² − 4 = 2t² + 5t − 3`\nafter substituting the cubic, and that is positive for `t > 1/2`, which\n`realRootPath_pi_gt` supplies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairGamma_pi_rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairGamma_pi_rel","kind":"theorem","line":823,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L823-L826","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairBeta_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairBeta_pi","kind":"theorem","line":818,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L818-L821","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.realRootPath_pi_gt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.realRootPath_pi_gt","kind":"theorem","line":809,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L809-L816","doc":"`t² + t − 1 > 0` at `φ = π`, i.e. `t > (√5−1)/2`. If `t² ≤ 1 − t` then\n`t³ ≤ t − t²`, while the cubic gives `t³ = 1 + t − 2t²`; together they force\n`t² ≥ 1`, against `t < 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.realRootPath_pi_cubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.realRootPath_pi_cubic","kind":"theorem","line":802,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L802-L807","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuousAt_re_deformedV_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuousAt_re_deformedV_comp","kind":"theorem","line":774,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L774-L793","doc":"**`Re deformedV` along a path**, under the four conditions its four terms\nneed. Stated for arbitrary `X Y` so it can be applied at each of the three\nbranches without repetition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuousAt_re_log_neg_sq_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuousAt_re_log_neg_sq_comp","kind":"theorem","line":760,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L760-L772","doc":"`Re ∘ (log(−·)²) ∘ g`, likewise. `−g φ ∈ slitPlane` is the ordinary case;\n`0 < Re (g φ)` is the one where `−g φ` sits **on** log's cut and only the real\npart of the square survives (`re_log_neg_sq`). The real branch `Yreal > 0` is\nalways in the second case, and never in the first. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuousAt_re_cLiTwoExt_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuousAt_re_cLiTwoExt_comp","kind":"theorem","line":746,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L746-L758","doc":"`Re ∘ cLiTwoExt ∘ g` is continuous at `φ` when `g φ` is off the cut, or is a\nreal number **strictly** greater than 1. The branch point `1` itself is in\nneither case, and is not covered — deliberately, since `cLiTwoExt` is genuinely\nsingular in its derivative there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.envelopeS_total_concrete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.envelopeS_total_concrete","kind":"theorem","line":715,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L715-L733","doc":"**The transport, reduced to continuity alone.**\n\nGiven a collision point `c` and continuity of `S` on the closed interval, the\nwhole of `S(π) − S(0) = π²` follows. Every other hypothesis\n`hasDerivAt_envelopeS` and `envelopeS_total` between them asked for is now a\ntheorem about the concrete labelling.\n\n⚠ What is *not* here: `hcont`. Its hard point is `φ = π`, where two of the `Li₂`\narguments land on the cut — the `Li₂` half of that is proved\n(`continuousAt_re_cLiTwoExt`, 2-D), but composing it along the arc is not\nwritten. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.envelopeS_total_of_ioo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.envelopeS_total_of_ioo","kind":"theorem","line":706,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L706-L713","doc":"**The transport, with the endpoint hypothesis removed.** Same conclusion as\n`envelopeS_total`, with `Ico` weakened to `Ioo`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.total_of_deriv_on_ioo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.total_of_deriv_on_ioo","kind":"theorem","line":685,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L685-L704","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_envelopeS_concrete_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_envelopeS_concrete_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":654,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L654-L666","doc":"**`S′ = 2φ` on all of `Ioo 0 π` except the collision.**\n\nThe two regimes joined. `pairDisc φ ≠ 0` is exactly \"not at the collision\", and\nit is the *only* hypothesis left besides being in the open interval — the\nlabelling, the branch routing, the envelope condition and both log sums are all\ndischarged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_envelopeS_concrete_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_envelopeS_concrete_real","kind":"theorem","line":636,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L636-L652","doc":"**`S′ = 2φ` on the real-pair regime `Ioo φ₀ π`.** The mirror of\n`hasDerivAt_envelopeS_concrete`, with `pairDisc φ < 0` replaced by `0 < pairDisc φ`\nthroughout. Together the two cover `Ioo 0 π` minus the collision, which is\nexactly what `envelopeS_total_of_ioo` consumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_log_neg_Ypair_snd_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_log_neg_Ypair_snd_real","kind":"theorem","line":627,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L627-L634","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_log_neg_Ypair_fst_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_log_neg_Ypair_fst_real","kind":"theorem","line":618,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L618-L625","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.neg_Ypair_mem_slitPlane_of_disc_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.neg_Ypair_mem_slitPlane_of_disc_pos","kind":"theorem","line":611,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L611-L616","doc":"On the real branch `−y` is a **positive real**, so it is in `slitPlane` by\n`Re > 0` rather than by `Im ≠ 0` — the opposite disjunct from the complex case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_envelopeS_concrete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_envelopeS_concrete","kind":"theorem","line":582,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L582-L609","doc":"**`S′ = 2φ` at the concrete labelling.**\n\n`hasDerivAt_envelopeS` took fourteen hypotheses about an arbitrary labelling;\nall fourteen are now theorems about `Yreal` / `Ypair`, and this is what closes\nGap A's construction half.\n\n⚠ **`Ioo 0 π`, and the two ends fail for different reasons.** At `φ = π` `VSide`\nis FALSE (`x·y = 2.2469796` on Li₂'s cut, Route 36 G7) and so is `heⱼ`\n(`argSum = 2π`, Route 38 G15) — that end is genuinely out of reach and\n`envelopeS_total` is built not to need it. At `φ = 0` the *statement* is fine —\n`arcX 0 = 1`, so `hA` and `hB` reduce to `∏(1−yⱼ) = 1` and the conjugate pair's\narguments cancel — but three inputs (`vSide_*`, `logSumA_concrete`,\n`logSumB_concrete`) carry `sin φ ≠ 0` and do not reach it. That is a gap in the\n*route*, not in the mathematics, and it is the one thing between this and\n`envelopeS_total`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.he_Yreal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.he_Yreal","kind":"theorem","line":571,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L571-L580","doc":"**`heⱼ` at the real branch.** No `k`-pinning is needed here and that is not an\naccident: `arg y ≡ 0` along a real branch, so the `2πi·k` leak is annihilated by\n`Y′` being real whatever `k` is. It is the pair, where `arg y` moves, that forced\n`k = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_Yreal'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_Yreal'","kind":"theorem","line":564,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L564-L569","doc":"`Yreal`'s derivative in the form the transport consumes — the same statement\nas `hasDerivAt_Yreal`, with the value written as `realRootPath'` rather than\nexpanded, so it matches `hasDerivAt_log_neg_Yreal`'s numerator on the nose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.logSumB_concrete_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.logSumB_concrete_real","kind":"theorem","line":538,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L538-L556","doc":"`hB` on the real branch — identical to `logSumB_concrete` except that the two\n`Im(y/x)` sign facts come from `re_Ypair_neg_of_disc_pos` rather than from the\nconjugacy, which does not hold here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.he_Ypair_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.he_Ypair_real","kind":"theorem","line":511,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L511-L536","doc":"**`heⱼ` on the real branch** — regime 4 of `FiveTwoPairSaddle`, where\n`arg(1−y)` and `arg(−y)` are both `0` outright and the whole quantity collapses\nto `arg(1−xy) + arg(1−y/x) ∈ (−π, π)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_mul_Ypair_neg_of_disc_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_mul_Ypair_neg_of_disc_pos","kind":"theorem","line":501,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L501-L509","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_div_Ypair_pos_of_disc_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_div_Ypair_pos_of_disc_pos","kind":"theorem","line":489,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L489-L499","doc":"The two `Im(y/x)` sign facts on the real branch — proved directly, not\nthrough the conjugacy `Ypair.2 = conj Ypair.1`, which is a complex-branch fact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.re_Ypair_neg_of_disc_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.re_Ypair_neg_of_disc_pos","kind":"theorem","line":473,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L473-L487","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairBeta_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairBeta_pos","kind":"theorem","line":453,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L453-L471","doc":"**`β > 0` past the collision**, hence both real roots negative.\n\nIf `β ≤ 0` then `2c ≥ t > 0`, so `β² = (2c−t)² ≤ (2−t)²` using `c ≤ 1`; and\n`4γ = 4/t > 4 > (2−t)²` for `t ∈ (0,1)`. So `pairDisc = β² − 4γ < 0`, against the\nhypothesis. No fact about where the discriminant crossing sits is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairGamma_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairGamma_pos","kind":"theorem","line":445,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L445-L451","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.he_Ypair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.he_Ypair","kind":"theorem","line":415,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L415-L431","doc":"**`heⱼ` at BOTH pair branches, for every `Y′`.**\n\n`∂V/∂y` is zero there, so the envelope condition holds outright rather than by\n`Y′` being annihilated — stronger than `hasDerivAt_envelopeS` asks for, and\nstrictly easier to use. Together with `re_dVdy_mul_eq_zero_of_real` at the real\nbranch, this discharges all three of `he₁ he₂ he₃`.\n\n⚠ `Ico 0 π`, never `Icc`. At `φ = π` this is **FALSE** — `argSum = 2π` there\n(Route 38 G15), for exactly the reason `VSide` fails: `x·y = 2.2469796` lands on\nLi₂'s cut, so `arg(1−xy)` and `arg(1−y/x)` are both `π` instead of cancelling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.dVdy_Ypair_snd_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.dVdy_Ypair_snd_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":395,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L395-L413","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.abs_argSum_Ypair_snd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.abs_argSum_Ypair_snd","kind":"theorem","line":387,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L387-L393","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arg_neg_Ypair_fst_ne_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arg_neg_Ypair_fst_ne_pi","kind":"theorem","line":377,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L377-L385","doc":"`arg(−y) ≠ π` at the pair — `−y` has non-zero imaginary part, and\n`arg_eq_pi_iff` needs it to vanish. One of `argSum_conj`'s four side conditions,\nand the only one not coming from `notCut`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.notCut_Ypair_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.notCut_Ypair_fst","kind":"theorem","line":361,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L361-L375","doc":"The three `notCut` memberships, on the **closed** left endpoint. Off `φ = 0`\nthey are `VSide`'s; at `φ = 0` all three collapse to `y ∈ notCut`, because\n`arcX 0 = 1`. `VSide` itself is unavailable there (`vSide_of_root` carries\n`x.im ≠ 0`), which is why this is not just `vSide_Ypair_fst`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.dVdy_Ypair_fst_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.dVdy_Ypair_fst_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":334,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L334-L350","doc":"**`∂V/∂y = 0` at the pair's first branch** — the last hypothesis\n`hasDerivAt_envelopeS` was still taking on faith.\n\n`exists_int_dVdy_mul` leaves an unpinned integer `k`; the four regime bounds pin\nit to `0`, and with `k = 0` the derivative vanishes outright rather than merely\nbeing annihilated by `Y′`. Stated on `Ico 0 π`, which is exactly what\n`envelopeS_total` consumes — and no wider: at `φ = π` this is **false**\n(`argSum = 2π`, Route 38 G15), for the same reason `VSide` fails there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.one_sub_ne_zero_Ypair_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.one_sub_ne_zero_Ypair_fst","kind":"theorem","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L317-L332","doc":"The three non-vanishing side conditions `dVdy_eq_zero_of_argSum_bound` needs,\non the **closed** left endpoint. Off `φ = 0` they come from `VSide`; at `φ = 0`\nall three collapse to `1 − y ≠ 0`, because `arcX 0 = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.eq_zero_of_sin_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.eq_zero_of_sin_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":311,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L311-L315","doc":"`sin φ = 0` on `[0, π)` pins `φ = 0` — the one place the `Ico` endpoint has\nto be argued rather than inherited. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arcX_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arcX_zero","kind":"theorem","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L306-L309","doc":"`arcX 0 = 1`. Needed because the transport starts at `φ = 0`, where `VSide`\nis unavailable (`vSide_of_root` carries `x.im ≠ 0`) and every `x`-dependent\nquantity collapses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.abs_argSum_Ypair_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.abs_argSum_Ypair_fst","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L265-L304","doc":"**`|argSum| < 2π` at the pair's first branch**, by the three-way dispatch.\n\n`Re y = cos φ − t/2` with `t > 0`, so `Re y > 0` *forces* `cos φ > 0` — that is\nwhat makes the case split three-way rather than four-way, and it is also why\n`im_mul_Ypair_fst_neg`'s `cos φ < 0` is not a gap: its failure region is exactly\nregime 1, where the opposite sign is what supplies the bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_div_Ypair_fst_pos'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_div_Ypair_fst_pos'","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L251-L263","doc":"The divisor sign fact, extended to the closed left endpoint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.re_arcX_mul_add_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.re_arcX_mul_add_div","kind":"theorem","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L244-L249","doc":"**The identity regime 3 runs on**: `Re(x·y) + Re(y/x) = 2cos φ·Re y`. No sign\nof an imaginary part appears in it, which is the point — regime 3 is where\nneither `Im` argument is available. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_arcX_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_arcX_div","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L238-L242","doc":"`Im(y/x) = cos φ·Im y − sin φ·Re y` on the arc — the *other* combination, and\nthe reason the two branches are not related by flipping one sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_arcX_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_arcX_mul","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L233-L236","doc":"`Im(x·y) = cos φ·Im y + sin φ·Re y` on the arc. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.normSq_arcX","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.normSq_arcX","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L228-L231","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_Ypair_fst_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_Ypair_fst_pos","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L224-L226","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairIm_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairIm_pos","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L220-L222","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_log_neg_Ypair_snd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_log_neg_Ypair_snd","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L191-L198","doc":"**`Y₃` takes route 1.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_log_neg_Ypair_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_log_neg_Ypair_fst","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L182-L189","doc":"**`Y₂` takes route 1.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.neg_Ypair_mem_slitPlane","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.neg_Ypair_mem_slitPlane","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L177-L180","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pair_im_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pair_im_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L164-L175","doc":"The pair is genuinely non-real off the collision — which is what puts `−Y₂`\nand `−Y₃` in `slitPlane` and so selects route 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_log_neg_Yreal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_log_neg_Yreal","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L152-L162","doc":"**`Y₁` takes route 2**, and needs no hypothesis at all.\n\n`hasDerivAt_log_neg_ofReal` is stated for a path of the form\n`fun u => ((t u : ℝ) : ℂ)`; `Yreal` is *definitionally* that, which is the whole\nreason it was built as the complexification of a real function rather than as a\n`ℂ`-valued function that happens to be real. `log_neg_route` says route 1 is\n**impossible** here — `−Y₁` is a negative real, squarely on `log`'s cut. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.logSumB_concrete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.logSumB_concrete","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L130-L148","doc":"**`hB` at the concrete labelling.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.logSumA_concrete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.logSumA_concrete","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L102-L128","doc":"**`hA` at the concrete labelling — and it needs NO off-collision hypothesis.**\n\nLean flagged `pairDisc φ < 0` as unused here, and that is a real asymmetry rather\nthan a slip. `logSumA`'s signs are `Im(x·y)` facts, which `im_mul_otherRoots_*`\nprove straight from the root structure. `logSumB`'s come *via conjugacy*\n(`im_div_eq_neg_im_mul_conj`), and the pair is only conjugate where\n`pairDisc φ < 0` — past the discriminant flip they are two distinct reals, each\nits own conjugate but not each other's. So `hA` survives the collision and `hB`\ndoes not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.one_sub_ne_zero_of_mem_notCut","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.one_sub_ne_zero_of_mem_notCut","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L93-L100","doc":"`w ∈ notCut → 1 − w ≠ 0`. `notCut` excludes `w = 1` — that point has `Im = 0`\nand `Re = 1`, failing both disjuncts — so the nonvanishing `logSumA`/`logSumB`\nwant comes free from `VSide`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.vSide_Ypair_snd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.vSide_Ypair_snd","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L82-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.vSide_Ypair_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.vSide_Ypair_fst","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L78-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.vSide_Yreal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.vSide_Yreal","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeInstance.lean#L74-L76","signatureChunk":0}]}